      "body": "This is unrelated, but pretty much every line here is problematic:\n\n* The default values are hard-coded a second time manually\n* The values are parsed as a singed int, but negative values are rejected manually\n\nI'd say all of this can be avoided by using `self.Arg<uint32_t>(\"count\")`. etc (or u64)\n\nPossibly there could be an early check for `AdditionOverflow<u64>(count,from)` and early exit, to avoid having to manually cast later on?",
