      },
      "body": "Thanks, done. `count` and `skip` now go through `self.Arg<uint64_t>`, so the duplicated defaults and the manual negative checks are gone.\n\nFor the sum I used `SaturatingAdd` rather than an early exit: something like `count=UINT64_MAX, skip=1` is a valid \"everything but the newest\" request, so returning early would give the wrong answer there. With the saturated limit the rest is plain unsigned `std::min`, no casts.\n\nNegative values now fail with \"JSON integer out of range\" (-1) instead of \"Negative count\"/\"Negative from\" (-8), same as other `Arg<uint*>` params. Test updated for that, plus a `UINT64_MAX` case. I left `listrawtransactions` alone to keep this small.\n",
